            <div xml:id="d351">

                <pb facs="0514" n="402" xml:id="pg402"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/7349: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-11-07T12:00:00+08:00">November 7,
                        1935—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received November 7—6:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>122. Embassy’s 121, November 6, 5 p.m. Chin Teh-chun, Acting Chairman of Chahar,
                    has been appointed Mayor of Peiping, and Hsiao Chen-ying has been given the
                    Chairmanship of Chahar. Both are close followers of Sung Che-yuan.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
